id: pm-context-r6x0
title: Decide whether to rewrite public git history to remove the maintainer's personal-domain commit identity
description: "The full commit-identity inventory contains a legacy personal-domain email identity. Rewrite the public repository history only with explicit maintainer approval, preserve tag and release semantics, coordinate the force update, and verify every ref contains only approved noreply and automation identities before any later publication."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 0
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-07T16:55:11.230Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T21:44:08.956Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: maintainer approves the coordinated history rewrite; every branch and tag is inventoried before mutation; rewritten refs contain only allowlisted noreply or automation identities; tags releases package provenance and clone instructions are verified after the force update; publication remains disabled until an independent privacy review approves the rewritten history
definition_of_ready: Maintainer selects approved replacement identity and maintenance window
reviewer: maintainer
risk: critical
confidence: high
release: blocked
severity: critical
expected_result: Public history contains no personal-domain author or committer identity
actual_result: "The maintainer's personal-domain identity appears in legacy and squash-merge commit metadata; it was later added to the fleet-wide approved identity allowlist, so gates pass, but it remains in public history"
affected_version: all reachable history through 2026.8.7
component: release privacy
customer_impact: Publication cannot satisfy the explicit no-personal-data history gate until remediated
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T12:25:42.910Z",codex-agent,"Triage at main 684a6fa (released package 2026.10.16): the historical identity is in the fleet-wide approved allowlist .github/approved-git-identities.txt. The forward-only policy is recorded in .github/identity-baseline.txt and enforced by test/identity-audit.test.ts. Any history rewrite requires explicit maintainer approval. No history changes requested or performed."
  "2026-10-16T14:27:34.095Z",claude-orchestrator,"Reconciled title and actual_result with the allowlist status (CodeRabbit on pm-context#150): the original finding (identity present in public history) stands; the allowlist only makes gates pass. Any history rewrite still needs explicit maintainer approval; raised to the maintainer in the 2026-10-16 session summary."
